      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An 84-year-old patient with a fracture of the humerus suffered from severe pain. Analgesia was not sufficient using opioids. Because of a chronic heart disease a blockade of the brachial plexus was used for analgesia without any technical examination. The necessity of different medical examinations before block performance will be discussed."},
